---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="About" description="About inteligenciaartificialdev.com — practical AI prompts and tool comparisons for developers.">
  <section class="container about">
    <h1>About AI DEV</h1>
    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        This site started from a practical problem: writing the same kind of
        prompt over and over while building software, and losing time
        reformulating something that should have already been ready to go.
      </p>
      <p>
        I'm a computer science instructor and systems analyst, and I build
        educational tools and AI products day to day — from question
        generators for public exams to AI-assisted essay grading platforms.
        This blog comes from that same instinct: turn a manual, repetitive
        process into something tested, documented, and reusable.
      </p>

      <h2>Our Mission</h2>
      <p>
        New models and tools ship every week, and most of what gets written
        about them is either marketing copy or hype. Our goal is to cut
        through that: test the prompt, run the comparison, and tell you
        plainly whether something is worth your time.
      </p>

      <h2>What We Cover</h2>
      <p>We create content for developers who actually use AI day to day, focusing on:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Prompt Engineering:</strong> tested prompts and techniques for real development tasks — debugging, refactoring, documentation, and more.</li>
        <li><strong>AI Coding Tools:</strong> honest comparisons between coding assistants, agents, and IDE integrations.</li>
        <li><strong>Tutorials:</strong> step-by-step guides for getting more out of the AI tools you already use.</li>
        <li><strong>Chatbots &amp; Model Releases:</strong> plain-English breakdowns of new model launches — what changed, what it costs, whether it matters.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Why Trust Us</h2>
      <p>
        Every prompt and workflow published here is tested against real code
        and real tasks before it goes up, not copy-pasted from a marketing
        page. Models change often, so we say when something is time-sensitive
        instead of presenting it as permanent truth.
      </p>

      <h2>Let's Connect</h2>
      <p>
        Questions, corrections, or a tool you think we should cover? Reach
        out through our <a href="/contact">contact page</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .about {
    padding-block: 56px 80px;
    max-width: 68ch;
  }

  .about h1 {
    margin-bottom: 32px;
  }
</style>
